bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A is a set in a Borel extended metric space and d is NNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M001-0009/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"a947775ad897312becd823a9fb1e711c7a465946060685c6d5f2ae9c56677d1d\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH.{u_1} : ∀ {X : Type u_1} [inst : EMetricSpace.{u_1} X] [inst_1 : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} X]\\\\n  [inst_2 :\\\\n    @BorelSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n      (@UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n        (@PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.{u_1} X (@EMetricSpace.toPseudoEMetricSpace.{u_1} X inst)))\\\\n      inst_1]\\\\n  {s : Set.{u_1} X} {d : NNReal},\\\\n  @LT.lt.{0} ENNReal (@Preorder.toLT.{0} ENNReal (@PartialOrder.toPreorder.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instPartialOrder)) (↑d)\\\\n      (@dimH.{u_1} X inst s) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@DFunLike.coe.{u_1 + 1, u_1 + 1, 1} (@MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} X inst_1) (Set.{u_1} X) (fun x => ENNReal)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike.{u_1} X inst_1)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure.{u_1} X inst inst_2 ↑d) s)\\\\n      (@Top.top.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instTop)\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"The integral of a countable sum of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"The integral of a countable sum of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"Countable index type; each summand is AEMeasurable ENNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M002-0008/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"254ede729428097ad087ac8d9763fdd9e9a429feaa566f7146c5293161f70d46\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Add\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"14da3dd3c269221e9ec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum.{u_1,\\\\n    u_2} : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {m : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {μ : @MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α m}\\\\n  [Countable.{u_2 + 1} β] {f : β → α → ENNReal},\\\\n  (∀ (i : β), @AEMeasurable.{u_1, 0} α ENNReal ENNReal.measurableSpace m (f i) μ) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a =>\\\\n        @tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace (fun i => f i a)\\\\n          (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\\n      (@tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace\\\\n        (fun i => @MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a => f i a) (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"dim_H\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let D=dim_H(E), F=E×I. Boundedness and cube coverings of a bounded Euclidean box show D≤n. For q>D, the definition gives H^q(E)=0. At scale δ cover E by positive-diameter r_j≤δ with arbitrarily small Σr_j^q, replacing singleton members by tiny balls with arbitrarily small total added cost. Cover I by ≤1/r_j+1 intervals of length ≤r_j; products have diameter ≤√2r_j and total (q+1)-cost ≤2(√2)^(q+1)Σr_j^q. Therefore dim_H(F)≤D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"r_j\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D>0 choose 0<s<D. M001 gives H^s(E)=∞, so scale contents c_s(E,δ)→∞. For any cover V_i of F at scale δ, put ρ_i=diam(V_i) and project to A_i,B_i. Enclose B_i in open intervals J_i with length ≤ρ_i+η_i and Ση_iρ_i^s<ε. For each t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E; thus c_s(E,δ)≤Σ1_{J_i}(t)ρ_i^s pointwise. Indicators are measurable nonnegative; M002 integrates this series to obtain c_s(E,δ)≤Σ(ρ_i+η_i)ρ_i^s≤Σρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Zero diameters contribute zero. Let ε→0 and infimize over covers; c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ), implying H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and dim_H(F)≥s+1. Let s↑D.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"s\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"V_i\\\",\\\"ρ_i\\\",\\\"A_i\\\",\\\"B_i\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"η_i\\\",\\\"ε\\\",\\\"c_s\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D=0 choose x₀∈E by H001. Projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz. Mapping covers by this map cannot increase diameters, so dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F). Direct interval length and subdivision estimates give dim_H(I)=1. Thus dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. This holds for n=0; combine upper and lower bounds.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"x₀\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply to E with 0<s<D in Euclidean Borel space.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Summands are ρ_i^s times indicators of open J_i, hence AEMeasurable on I.\\\"]}]}]}}\"}","status":"completed"}}

